# live_vs_offline.m8script — Task 5a
#
# Loads a fixture, renders it offline via the in-app render command.
# The WAV is then compared against m8_render's output of the same song
# using: m8_analyze --diff <in_app.wav> <m8_render.wav>
#
# Both paths call Engine::render() — the bar is exact sample-for-sample identity.
#
# The fixture MUST be audible, and must not need samples.
#
# This used V4EMPTY.m8s until 2026-08-14 — an EMPTY song, so both sides rendered
# silence, the hashes matched trivially, and `m8_analyze --diff` refused the
# comparison as identical inputs. The section passed on that for as long as it
# existed, which means ARCHITECTURE.md's hard invariant #11 (app and offline
# renderer produce identical audio) was never actually checked.
#
# HyperSynth.m8s renders at peak 0.398, crest 20 dB, and loads zero samples — so it
# needs no sample root, which matters because the manifest's `diff` policy has no
# field for one.

load tests/fixtures/device_golden/HyperSynth.m8s
assert_no_error
render 1 live_vs_offline_app.wav
assert_no_error
